# Since r>0, this bounds r above by its positive zero. The candidate below
# has discriminant zero, so it attains that bound and maximizes r.
# Also, E = 36 - 2660/(126-r), which decreases as r increases.
x = Q39(3, F(-1, 3))
y = x
